{"title":"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f813feeabb5d1046b6034e80f28c429a3638fd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{N}^{+}\\to\\mathbb{N}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f538b70912a3ca6364ac9e27e709aa042590a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" />\nis the set of positive integers. Prove that if\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/229494289e8704d1368c31101c1f844752159dab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n+1) &gt; f(f(n))\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d19f96e7aa389ed47ed3164ed7979e1e1c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will prove this via induction. First we will prove there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c90deec8b13a758a72dc4653420712840ab8a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and then that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd2a4ec9cf64d68580d5ef68252432965551b464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> is the only such solution.\n</p><p>Define the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba54b99b172d170fa6f5527e6cb748a787e0d7db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa599c60f9870a8bdeacbfab78597b1fed97d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ecb0ae4b7a24285173c6cd9ca4c76515f2e5b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=f(a_{k-1}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />. By the given inequality we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/2771b5d26193731a9d8c99e7ccf0325b6f93cefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_n)&gt;f(a_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, this can be used to form a inequality chain of decreasing positive integers: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/3126eb511dbb538573f5e68a2c9087e991e928f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a_0)&gt;f(a_1)&gt;f(a_2)&gt;...\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\nBy <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite_Descent\" title=\"Infinite Descent\">Infinite Descent</a>, this sequence must terminate, and the only way it can terminate is if we input something into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> that is outside of its range. This can only happen if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965a91ea46832772bbc200fe53dd6c0d102def67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> since the range and domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are the positive integers. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5144e5948bbd508809840db08ec8cca069da7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />, there is a integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1afe24d7e4984d552b698cce3f81c8a8f027ecdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c90deec8b13a758a72dc4653420712840ab8a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea5bca23bce54799fb4eaaddda8951745cb4c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950a0a8bb4631d12ec2abe7061b9e27c0523f817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=1&gt;f(f(t-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />, which is impossible since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934271f41a382980b7ba8db13a0d1bbc653cc344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(t-1))\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> by the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd2a4ec9cf64d68580d5ef68252432965551b464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> is the only time when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c90deec8b13a758a72dc4653420712840ab8a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now for the inductive step.\n</p><p>Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d19f96e7aa389ed47ed3164ed7979e1e1c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b8509880feedf248af3be52483dd593c83fad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and these are the only times these values occur. We will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83ffe7f081bfaaca429cf1f3c1c33abf88744951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> and that this is the only time this value occurs. Define the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> similarly, except that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d647ce8a9efc680a9eb29d0f95e1ecf00517303c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0&gt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, by the reasoning above, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddf57a1507686a49e3d290b3542ccac565cd35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fcee86eeeb00fcd68ac53fa56a33ec3b4601de3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_m)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, by the inductive assumption, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de6b465e967a384f518462cc08e1b463410377eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m=f(a_{m-1}-1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />, we can repeat the inductive assumption to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d5b610e4ac5d6e4a3806f98e2d0ccc987dbc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m-k+1}=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1ab9f9dcc012b58ff899fc21f485bb7179c1815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a_{m-k}-1)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312a14d1dcc48f4908d9450d03490b20ffe2147e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now for that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9306f5dd7060042edcb5da3f2d98beb97c45e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;f(f(t-1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e518817dfcc42f865c75f3eb322bb1ae04c4ca8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1&gt;t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> by the inductive assumption which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a132794840a4caa831389ba6a8a3a6b50272ffda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> since we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/2417a40b694f02b045be6a831ce7a10966038af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t&gt;k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5cb6388721f8a24beab604acd21bbd26ffcf19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a132794840a4caa831389ba6a8a3a6b50272ffda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is the only time when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312a14d1dcc48f4908d9450d03490b20ffe2147e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So the inductive step is complete. Therefore, by induction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d19f96e7aa389ed47ed3164ed7979e1e1c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly increasing.\n</p><p>To prove this, we will prove by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054a7ad7af69c3dfe33d62ae87fb21cdb93e6895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) &lt; f(2) &lt; \\dots &lt; f(k) \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24f7be369653b41d301d63cc07d6fcbd4ef9f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &gt; f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463156309b94b2e71f0821563e8ed5acfb6d0855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge k + 1 \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>First, prove the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. There is nothing to prove for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b2f6f4ce90e90850b14e6b2a1c58c48a7d7258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" />.\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31dc0a1581ed5f7534c1a90af4b15e05b305ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84a5f634f92dd95dc2cba75e13ef53435288f75c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\min\\{f(n), n \\ge 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />. We will show that if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbb592a6e98fb68fe46a858269a44b36b3f91d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361ea4cb174e2c033a0a888475e35613e4aa3765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc86688cd9e5a4ce262df69345bacac9f89f8ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Then we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b222a720669a55f4334d4504a214db4e7ad957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b222a720669a55f4334d4504a214db4e7ad957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />\nis in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f210b79b44ba0f06662d484e9c142ae4f05bed6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, so we can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b774c9534368acdb1d429f7f317723c1c4888b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(p - 1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd4ac88b6ecc5c5c6e788ffacfdb26a22cbce54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le f(f(p - 1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" /> because of the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebea496212cd09e3161ebe6398f509e46bb44ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(p - 1)) &lt; f(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\nby hypothesis, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbb592a6e98fb68fe46a858269a44b36b3f91d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> because of the choice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Putting\nit all together, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b350dfa7bfc6bc3e8dfd957b4419f6471d9496da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le f(f(p - 1)) &lt; f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />, which implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfdfd7d1051dadaea9fede2476306e060d2d692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. This contradiction tells us that the assumption <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc86688cd9e5a4ce262df69345bacac9f89f8ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is\nfalse, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361ea4cb174e2c033a0a888475e35613e4aa3765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let us now assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/3724e8561ed5cc0c1ecee6f0b4687e1a5dafacb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a), (b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and prove them for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c67ea5aa91b3396c2614de7a02fc04b4dd6ac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\{n, n \\ge k + 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbeb35e07196962f862757b5d8d7a50b039f2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\min\\{f(n), n \\in M\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />\n(in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3accb9ca80d901845f5869da69003447628d5fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\min\\{f(n), n \\ge k + 1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />). Choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc4457fbe6c57c7945ae191fde7c63530d291f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\in M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />\nsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbb592a6e98fb68fe46a858269a44b36b3f91d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. We will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf7c2dca0df22d81f57632c3e0a6a8dd8f558f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b2f6f4ce90e90850b14e6b2a1c58c48a7d7258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> says <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c6b1fb34c34bd78686736083f1db9350809a45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) &lt; f(2) &lt; \\dots &lt; f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />; we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5c6f33c6c91ff8a21986fdae8475980176ba42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k) \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />.\n(Indeed, if we have a strictly increasing sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> numbers,\nthe last one has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a672502b5e67a817894033cc6787b1931701bf60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p><p>Note that because of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31dc0a1581ed5f7534c1a90af4b15e05b305ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f53245af337df5d0afe6dc0683766745cb9f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />. (Indeed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19da498ce81d7b0d16cef9301ed028d004b23c4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = f(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />\nfor a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03a934f91e3f9d8c8adb4c9ee8fee6ad6300b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ge k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.)\n</p><p>Now suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d5e9505a3025bba8992997f49f5ebe3090230e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/5743df5242a5b652fb8e9928ec6b842f5bf3f27c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1 \\in M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, so if we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b222a720669a55f4334d4504a214db4e7ad957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />,\nwe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7fffe306c1a125f7f4f106b5ba6886784316e90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1) \\ge m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Putting the last three inequalities together, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/29260de771e93cb128fb69af54fa9452e4993706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1) \\ge m &gt; f(k) \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />, in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0ddc0daa9416ad256bacf03a4a6a950f63d3e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1) &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891be0733194111ded4272afad81d0468e5f2fbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1) \\in M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2c73e378262fa20eff7647682f5ffa3464c9d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p - 1) \\ge k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />).\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd4ac88b6ecc5c5c6e788ffacfdb26a22cbce54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le f(f(p - 1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. Combine with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebea496212cd09e3161ebe6398f509e46bb44ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(p - 1)) &lt; f(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\n(from the hypothesis), and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbb592a6e98fb68fe46a858269a44b36b3f91d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> (from the choice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />) to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b350dfa7bfc6bc3e8dfd957b4419f6471d9496da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le f(f(p - 1)) &lt; f(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cfdfd7d1051dadaea9fede2476306e060d2d692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. This contradiction shows\nthat our assumption <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d5e9505a3025bba8992997f49f5ebe3090230e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> was wrong, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf7c2dca0df22d81f57632c3e0a6a8dd8f558f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b2f6f4ce90e90850b14e6b2a1c58c48a7d7258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31dc0a1581ed5f7534c1a90af4b15e05b305ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> follow from this.\n</p><p>Now we will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. From the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly\nincreasing, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1779c0e33f33a97be8290e4d2e1e34bc545268bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) \\ge n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> (we used this argument above). We\nwant to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff340d08c2ab55f046e779636ab6aa2fa4760179.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n + k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />,\nand suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172e6dadffd9800e796f3f96a1e24ce2a1840f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c8465da6fb947d9ebea187425dc9d8ea5d59cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n + 1) = f(f(n)) &lt; f(n + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"20\" /> (from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749992a18a3c07d4b41c5159ed7af859d55b4aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1 = f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />\nand the hypothesis), which is a contradiction.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e5fdee1c6d0e5b9100fd95c6e178d3d682ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &lt; f(n + 1) &lt; \\dots &lt; f(n + k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"298\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly increasing. Applying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> once more, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b90919898285ae4afbf6f96e607c388ae4d28511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(n)) &lt; f(f(n + 1)) &lt; \\dots &lt; f(f((n + k - 1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Combine with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997ad8661c5d85965830dbdb1046c0daec074c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + k = f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f01f8fca56bd083cef06222ebc4c3a99e5c7b91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(n + k - 1)) &lt; f(n + k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" /> (by\nhypothesis) and get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90d7c247b6eb1fffc138088ccfc426d35d723798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n + k) = f(f(n)) &lt; f(f(n + 1)) &lt; \\dots &lt; f(f(n + k - 1)) &lt; f(n + k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"558\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bb6a9ef4d603143dd5aecaec8abd4eba929643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n + k) &lt; f(n + k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />. This contradiction shows that\nthe assumption <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172e6dadffd9800e796f3f96a1e24ce2a1840f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> can not be true, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84574de7797bc7b4e1fc52075f4d265ba60a8bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, April 2026]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO\" title=\"1977 IMO\">1977 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1977 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041115\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.044 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 535/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 24292/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.578      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.578      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18584:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041115 and revision id 281681. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}